  "nl_text": "The schema \"rschema_0330\" is a database that stores information about users, user identities, roles, and role associations. The database has five tables: \"user,\" \"user_identity_key,\" \"user_and_identity_key_association,\" \"role,\" and \"role_and_role_association.\"\nThe \"user\" table contains information about individual users, including their ID, version, user name, user name case-insensitive, password hash, status, email address, email address case-insensitive, display name, display name case-insensitive, locale tag, time zone, date format style, and time format style. The table has a primary key on the \"id\" column.\nThe \"user_identity_key\" table contains information about user identities, including their ID, key scheme, and key value. The table has a primary key on the \"id\" column.\nThe \"user_and_identity_key_association\" table contains information about the association between users and user identities. The table has a primary key on the \"user_id\" and \"id_key_id\" columns, and it has foreign key constraints on the \"id_key_id\" column that references the \"user_identity_key\" table, and on the \"user_id\" column that references the \"user\" table. The foreign key constraints have the ON DELETE CASCADE and ON UPDATE CASCADE options.\nThe \"role\" table contains information about roles, including their ID, version, role name, role name case-insensitive, and description. The table has a primary key on the \"id\" column.\nThe \"role_and_role_association\" table contains information about the association between roles and users. The table has a primary key on the \"id\" column, and it has foreign key constraints on the \"role_id\" column that references the \"role\" table, and on the \"user_id\" column that references the \"user\" table. The foreign key constraints have the ON DELETE CASCADE and ON UPDATE CASCADE options.\nIn summary, the schema \"rschema_0330\" is a database that stores information about users, user identities, roles, and role associations. The database has five tables that are related to each other through foreign key constraints, and the tables have primary keys and unique constraints to ensure data integrity.",
  "gold_question": "Business requirement description of the user management system: The system is used to manage user information, role information, and the association between users and roles. Each user has a unique user ID, username, password hash, status, email address, display name, language tag, time zone, date and time format, and other information. Each user can have multiple identity keys, each of which includes an authentication scheme and an identity key value. The system supports the creation and management of roles, and each role has a unique role ID, role name, and description. Relationships are established between users and roles through association tables. A role can be assigned to multiple users, and a user can also have multiple roles. The system records the user's basic information, identity keys, role assignments, and the relationship between users and roles in order to implement permission management and user authentication.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0330.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0330\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `version` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `user_name_ci` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password_hash` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `email_address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email_address_ci` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `display_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `display_name_ci` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `locale_tag` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `time_zone` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `date_format_style` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `time_format_style` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_identity_key` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `key_scheme` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `key_value` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_and_identity_key_association` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `id_key_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `id_key_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_and_identity_key_association_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_and_identity_key_association_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`id_key_id`) REFERENCES `user_identity_key` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `role` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `version` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `role_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `role_name_ci` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `role_and_role_association` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `role_and_role_association_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`role_id`) REFERENCES `role` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `role_and_role_association_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
